{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T09:35:59.020Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"72bc6070cdf8e143b3ffadf4","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-3627y1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The user-at-private-host secret rule rescans every hyphen or dot run, so 32 KB of hyphenated text costs about a second in mutation preflight"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-12 while answering a Codex review of pm-gh1704. The pre-existing user_at_private_host rule in src/core/shared/secret-rules.ts is a word boundary followed by [A-Za-z0-9._-]+@ and a private address. Every '-' or '.' inside a long run creates a new word boundary, so the engine restarts the greedy run at each one and the scan is quadratic in the run length. Measured with findSecretRuleMatches on credential-free input: 'a-' repeated 16,000 times takes about 1,169 ms, 'token-' repeated 8,000 times about 966 ms; every other rule stays under 20 ms. The rule runs synchronously in mutation preflight (advise mode included) and in the repository scan, so a pasted log can stall the CLI or a shared MCP process. Fix: start the local part only at the beginning of a run, for example a negative lookbehind for [A-Za-z0-9._-], keeping detection of a run that starts with a dot or hyphen, and add a linear-time regression test like the one pm-gh1704 added for credential_key_assignment."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["performance","regex","secret-guard","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-12T09:35:59.020Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T09:35:59.020Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":45},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Scanning 32 KB of hyphenated or dotted text with user_at_private_host finishes in linear time (well under 100 ms); Every existing user_at_private_host detection, including a local part that starts with a dot or hyphen, still matches in both the SDK guard and the repository scan; A regression test bounds the scan time"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Secret scanning cost stays linear in input size for every rule"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"user_at_private_host takes about a second on 32 KB of hyphenated text"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1704","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-12T09:35:59.020Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"079f5f61a8d01720dffc1636a656662d1701c2c4014b89053cf80c1845c83699","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"442f5aff34697f3716c9c264ea032939210a85457c6780227fa290d8b65d0985"}
